OL,3,ABloodied, dazed and angry - how
OL,4,Apassengers' rail journey turned to
OL,5,Adisaster in Spain
OL,6,
OL,7,FIt was approaching 08:30 (07:30 GMT) on
OL,8,Fa normal Wednesday. Two high-speed
OL,9,Ftrains were travelling south from the
OL,10,FSpanish capital, Madrid, to Seville.
OL,12,FOne, run by state-owned operator Renfe
OL,13,Fhad 397 passengers on board. Ahead of
OL,14,Fit on the same line was a train of Iryo
OL,15,Fprivate operator with 147 passengers. A
OL,16,Freported issue with the automatic
OL,17,Fsignalling system - a computer failure
OL,18,F- had forced all trains to halt on the
OL,19,Faffected stretch.
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/38
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
